<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moroccan Army of Liberation</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moroccan Army of Liberation was an irregular force formed in 1955 to fight French and Spanish colonial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. After Moroccan independence in 1956 it continued operations in the Spanish-held south, attacking Ifni and Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifni-war">Ifni War</a> of 1957-1958. It was later dissolved, many of its fighters joining the Moroccan army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moroccan-army-of-liberation.jpg" alt="Moroccan Army of Liberation" width="320" height="284" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abjiklam · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Sahara_conflict_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
